{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Kappaṭakura","html":"<article id='thag2.40'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 2.40 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 2.40 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Dukanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Twos </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Catutthavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Four </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Kappaṭakurattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Kappaṭakura </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Ayamiti kappaṭo kappaṭakuro, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>This chap, “Rag-rice”, he sure is a rag! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Acchāya atibharitāya; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Into the vase of freedom from death, <j>polished and overflowing, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Amataghaṭikāyaṁ dhammakaṭamatto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>sufficient teaching has been poured; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Katapadaṁ jhānāni ocetuṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the path to build up absorptions has been laid out. </span></span></p>\n<p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mā kho tvaṁ kappaṭa pacālesi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Don’t nod off, Rag—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Mā tvaṁ upakaṇṇamhi tāḷessaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I’ll smack your ear! </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na hi tvaṁ kappaṭa mattamaññāsi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>You know no limit, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saṅghamajjhamhi pacalāyamāno”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>nodding off in the midst of the Saṅgha! </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Kappaṭakuro thero … </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>vaggo catuttho. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Migasiro sivako ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>upavāṇo ca paṇḍito; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Isidinno ca kaccāno, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>nitako ca mahāvasī; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Poṭiriyaputto nisabho, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>usabho kappaṭakuroti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
